** Conclusion 


BBC and AI-generated passages differ in the variety, flexibility, and distribution of rhetorical relations.
The BBC passage develops roughly:Evidence, Elaboration, Cause, Contrast, Background, and Attribution-like information.
Importantly, these relations do not remain fixed within one section: the writer repeatedly changes the function of sentences as the discussion develops.
In Contrast AI-generated passage the rhetorical relations appear to be distributed less dynamically.
Within longer sections, the text often continues elaborating on the same point through several sentences before moving to a new rhetorical purpose.
As a result, the tree can contain long sequences of similar relations rather than the more frequent changes observed in the BBC passag
The AI passage develops roughly expert assessment → declining resilience → camel adaptations → limits of adaptation → environmental changes → biological consequences
But this structure also can be because of the detailed promt.

Another important feature of the BBC passage is the frequent use of source-based and evidential material.
These sources are not simply added as separate information; they are integrated into the rhetorical development of the text. 
A claim can therefore be followed by a quotation, statistical finding, explanation, or scientific interpretation that gives the reader a more specific reason to accept or understand the preceding information
